windowLoopT -- windows stroke 4 (SEQ 751, 2026-11-22): the loop (W1), the display's size, and show deciding between a
window and the PDF (Tony, 2026-11-22). A delta of tabClickT's preamble (copied, then patched). Rows in
genLadder/formsPop.sh, run at GCSTRESS=1000. No window is shown.

WL-SIZE before   displaySize is 0 by 0 until a window is laid out; fitCap is a page, 792.
WL-TWO           two windows open at once, each made and returned from at once, each read: tabForm's card green, wlSmall
                 red, each with its own title.
WL-SIZE after    displaySize holds the display less menu bar and dock (its values are this machine's; the row asks only
                 that both are more than 0), and fitCap is 792 again.
WL-TALL          a height=fit form whose members need 6000: in a window it is capped at the display's usable height
                 (the window's height equals displaySize.height, compared in formsPop), where a PDF caps at 792.
WL-SHOW          show decides. windows is 0: show(tkLoose), a form written window, goes to its PDF. windows = 2: the same
                 show makes a window (not shown; windows = 1 shows it) and writes no PDF. show(wlSmall), a form not written
                 window, still goes to its PDF.
WL-LAST          the script's last line prints: every opening returned.
THE LOOP         windowClick and three windowCloses carry `later`, so they are kept and done INSIDE the loop. stop() ends
                 the script; the loop starts (3 open, 0 shown, 4 kept); the click finds tabThree and runs kant -- tabClick
                 and selectTab, neither run before in this process -- after "stop: end parsing"; the three windows close,
                 each keeping its frame; the loop ends with none open and the process exits 0.
NOT HERE: a shown window. With one, the loop runs until the last shown window is closed by hand (stroke 5).
